				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7850308#post-4018319</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7850308/scp-069-ua#post-4018319</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Oct 2018 02:12:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>LadyKatie</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2150500</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I love the mental image of an iron that loves Soviet Communist music, to the point of getting in a loudness war with a songbird and a Beatles song. Having it discovered on a creepypasta site is kinda meta and really fun in a weird way, and I'm keeping in-universe creepypasta.</p> <p>I've heard people say that tools are a reflection of their owner. Makes you wonder.</p> <p>+1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7850308#post-4018289</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7850308/scp-069-ua#post-4018289</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Oct 2018 01:12:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>NatVoltaic</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2800867</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This definitely is rough around the edges &#8212; for an object with a fairly simple effect there's more description than is probably needed &#8212; and some of the translation is iffy, but at the same time there's a certain Series I charm that comes through that keeps me enjoying this. Also, thinking about using this to generate electricity is clever.</p> <p>+1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
